CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal

Preamble

CERN has developed this licence to promote collaboration among hardware designers
and to provide a legal tool which supports the freedom to use, study, modify,
share and distribute hardware designs and products based on them.

This CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal (“CERN-OHL-W”) applies
to the distribution of hardware designs and products. It is a “weakly reciprocal”
licence, meaning that modifications to the licensed material itself must be made
available under the same licence, but larger works incorporating the licensed
material may be distributed under different terms.

1. Definitions

“Licence” means this CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Weakly Reciprocal.

“Licensor” means any person or entity that distributes the Material under this Licence.

“You” means any natural or legal person exercising rights under this Licence.

“Material” means the hardware design files, documentation, schematics, PCB layouts,
BOMs and other information made available under this Licence.

“Product” means any device or physical object that is manufactured using the Material.

“Modification” means any alteration of, or addition to, the Material.

“Available Component” means any component which is commercially available and
does not need to be designed or modified in order to be used in a Product.

2. Licence Grant

The Licensor hereby grants You a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive licence to:

a) use, reproduce, study and modify the Material;
b) manufacture Products using the Material;
c) distribute the Material and Products.

3. Conditions

3.1 Distribution of Material
If You distribute the Material, You shall do so under the terms of this Licence and
shall provide access to the complete corresponding Material, including any Modifications,
in a form suitable for making further Modifications.

3.2 Distribution of Products
If You distribute a Product:
a) You shall provide recipients with information on how to obtain the complete
corresponding Material for that Product;
b) You may distribute the Product under terms of Your choice, provided that this
Licence is respected for the Material itself.

3.3 Modifications
If You make Modifications to the Material, those Modifications must be made available
under this Licence when You distribute them.

4. No Warranty

The Material is provided “as is” and without any express or implied warranties,
including, without limitation, warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular
purpose, or non-infringement. The entire risk as to the use of the Material is with You.

5. Limitation of Liability

In no event shall the Licensor be liable for any damages arising from the use,
modification or distribution of the Material or Products, including but not limited to
direct, indirect, incidental, consequential or special damages.

6. Applicable Law and Jurisdiction

This Licence shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of
Switzerland. Any dispute arising under or in connection with this Licence shall be
subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts of Geneva, Switzerland.

7. Versioning

This Licence is version 2.0 of the CERN Open Hardware Licence - Weakly Reciprocal.
The Licensor may choose to distribute the Material under later versions of the
CERN Open Hardware Licence as published by CERN.
